        {
          time: 'Morning',
          icon: '🌅',
          title: 'Upper & Lower Circuits',
          text: 'Enter the Parque Nacional Iguazú (ARS 28,000 for foreigners) as the gates open at 8am. Start with the Circuito Superior (Upper Circuit) — a 1.7km boardwalk above the falls with panoramic views of the cascades plunging into the gorge below. The mist, rainbows, and roar are immediate and overwhelming. Then take the Circuito Inferior (Lower Circuit) — 1.4km of steps and platforms that take you down to the base of the falls, face-to-face with walls of water.',
          tip: 'Arrive at park opening (8am) to beat the crowds and get the best light. The Lower Circuit gets you drenched — waterproof your phone and wear quick-dry clothes.',
